{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 6e9acc3a3f598a2ff1a275ebe6d8b166e0cb0f50 on builder/nf9-name-join-failure-20261117, all 10 artifacts, for request 8f55e67c under my promise 1af2294a. The implementation is NF-9 (request a75440d3, promise 1d8c7209). The reporting artifact is the NF-9 note. Main f197a89d is an ancestor.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The note first, then the whole diff.\n- `witness-request-shape.mjs`. `requestShape` keeps the method (or `OTHER`), the host, and the path with each `sc_` id marked `\u003cscope\u003e`, each `sha256:` digest marked `\u003cdigest\u003e`, and any segment that does not match `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,24}$` marked `\u003cid\u003e`. It keeps sorted query key names with no values, and an outcome that is an integer status, a `net::` name of at most 48 capitals, or `failed`. It gives null for an address that is not http or https. `recordRequests` listens for `requestfinished` and `requestfailed` on the context and keeps at most 400 shapes, counting the rest.\n- `custody-witness.mjs`. The hosted run attaches the recorder to the Counter context. On a stop, the private failure note holds the error and then the request lines. The note runs through the NF-8 `redact` with the run's secrets, and the witness writes it with mode 0600 and flag `wx`.\n- `enrollment-step.ts`. `atStep` wraps one step and rethrows any throw as an `EnrollmentStepError` with that step and a bounded class name, unless an inner step already named itself. `errorClass` uses the same name pattern as AS-2 and gives `other` or `non-error` otherwise. `unconfirmedWords` builds the page text from the step and the class only.\n- `installed.ts` and `main.ts`. The join-record load, save and clear, the browser key, the enrollment request, and the custody load and save each run inside `atStep`. The catch-all in `main.ts` now shows `unconfirmedWords(error)`. The `at === active` checks and their order do not change.\n- `release-identifiers.json` moves the open Counter 0.6.0 presentation from `c4275588` to `76ad09f8`. Counter 0.6.0 is unsigned, so ruling 163de663 allows the move.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- The reds. `2026-11-17-nf9-red/` holds two runs. The request-shape run without marks fails 2 cases and passes 3. The enrollment-step run without names fails 2 cases and passes 55.\n- The gate. END 5bcac92c passed at this head. The last lines of `gate.txt` read \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\".\n- Scope. The 10 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only f197a89d 6e9acc3a`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n- Wake rate. The head adds no alarm, retry or scheduled pass.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The witness names a failed request without a new signing, and the page names the failed step in the open version. The two changes answer different questions, and the note says which one runs against hosted 0.5.0. Run 4 (c2c171d3) already used this witness: every room request answered 200, so the stop is local to the browser. NF-10 owns that cause.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding.\n\n- A request shape keeps no query value, header or body. An invitation token or any other long path segment becomes `\u003cid\u003e`, and a test proves it for an `artroom-invite:` token. Host labels longer than 24 characters also become `\u003cid\u003e`.\n- The private note stays at mode 0600, and the witness redacts it with the run's secrets before writing.\n- The page shows only the step and a bounded class name. `EnrollmentStepError` keeps the original message for code, and no path in this head shows or sends it.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The recorder adds a `requestfinished` shape after `response()` resolves, but it adds a `requestfailed` shape at once. The note's \"oldest first\" therefore means oldest finished first, not oldest sent. A later head can record the send order if a run needs it.\n\nT